  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The newly discovered rank eight true inheritance at the fire thunder river segment of red dragon river was set up by Fire Thunder Divine Lord. He cultivates fire path primarily with lightning path secondarily. Though a lone cultivator, he had above average luck and many fortuitous encounters. He is not a Southern Border Gu Immortal; he came from Western Desert. After causing chaos there and being chased by several super forces, he reached the fire thunder river segment with injuries that could not heal, and before dying he made his arrangements.",
      "chapters": [
        2100
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_western_desert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His methods were close to nature. Over time the segment became the fire thunder river segment, producing fire path and lightning path Gu worms but never Immortal Gu, so Ba clan and Xia clan at that boundary paid little attention. The rank eight true inheritance stayed hidden until qi tides unveiled it, drawing almost all of Southern Border’s super clans until Wu clan, Ba clan, and Xia clan remained. Wu Yong later presents a Western Desert Gu Master as Fire Thunder Divine Lord’s bloodline inheritor when competing for that legacy.",
      "chapters": [
        2100
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
